  {
   "id": 335534,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/a5931cc56dc06b86.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n(credit: modification of work by Pomerantz A, et al./Med Hypotheses)\n</figure>\n",
   "stem_html": "<p>The image shows the olfactory system for a canine.</p>\n<p>Which is a testable hypothesis that can be written on the canine olfactory system based on this image?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 847724,
     "content_html": "Dogs breeds with larger tongues tend to have better olfactory sense."
    },
    {
     "id": 847725,
     "content_html": "Dog breeds whose olfactory nerves connect to the brain tend to have better olfactory sense."
    },
    {
     "id": 847726,
     "content_html": "Dog breeds with larger nostrils tend to have better olfactory sense."
    },
    {
     "id": 847727,
     "content_html": "Dogs breeds with larger snouts tend to have better olfactory sense."
    }
   ],
